Wrong. I often play character that as soon as I get down into the mines
I try to burden myself to get my con up by exercise and if I don't eat
corpses I *will* run out of food, whereas if you aren't burdened, you
can run around any level and gain food - otherwise no one would ever get
past the problem of fainting to say nothing of ascending. As for the
last that all depends on strength, and with a wizard which we *are*
talking about here, it can be *low*, I've seen as low as 8 to start, to
say nothing of being poisoned later on to drop it even further. In this
case the strength and con were 13 and 14, but I don't believe we ever
got an inventory list, so weight is an unknown, although the status line
doesn't *say* burdened. 

Naturally a lot of what I'm saying is in general term and not just
specific to this case. I notice that the character has played for over
3000 moves. By that point I usually have 50 hp 0 ac and expert in
quarterstaff and can safely run around the mines killing whatever comes
to me Even if it means non-leather armor, the point is to get ac down
and fighting ability. Buying protection because it only costs 400 z per
shot is deceiving. I've see several of post of newbies who seem to
*always* try the protection run and never seem to get past sokoban
despite having played for a year. Not very good odds. 

This is a diservice both to the popularization of the game and to those
players. Nethack can be a *lot* easier if you just use armor and
fighting. There is a *big* difference between basic and skilled in a
weapon in terms of survivability in the early game and sooner or later
spell points run out and in the early game you're toast if you can't
fight. 


I'm not saying *never* to go for protection, but the amount of money you
get in the game only goes up. by the time you get to ludios, you can
easily buy protection without doing anything more than picking it up and
the occasional vault. People either don't seem to realize this or never
get this far. -15 a.c will do you fine to to bottom of the mines and
quite likely the massive killing at the entrance of ludios at least - I
know I have done it myself. You can get that without buying protection
very easily. So When do you need protection? Obviously you quite likely
need it for the ascention. If you have a non-dragon non-enhanced ac of 0
- easy enough just from stuff you'll find in the mines, then this could
be enhanced to -20 just by judicious use of blank scrolls, magic
markers, holy water and uncursed scrolls of enchant armor. So what *do*
you need in ac anyways? 

I believe I've made my point - there's lots of stuff around, you just
got to be patient and collect it when you get to it and not worrying
about being -15 before 10000 moves or something silly like that. 

